<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#riau-malay">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Riau Malay</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/riau">Riau</a> Malay is the variety of Malay spoken in the Riau archipelago and the old Johor-Riau sultanate. Cultivated as a literary language at the Riau-Lingga court in the 19th century, it was taken by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> colonial scholars as the standard form of Malay, and it later became the basis of the Indonesian national language.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/riau-malay.jpg" alt="Riau Malay" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Irfansyah00 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Melayu_Traditional_Wedding.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
